        "A practical way to revisit When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next audit cycle is to pick the exception first and work back to the rule. The right choice depends on the team's size, the complexity of the accounts, and the need for continuity. A simple rotation may suit a team with similar accounts and a short sales cycle. A more deliberate assignment may suit a team with named accounts and long relationships. Ask a reviewer who did not prepare the item to restate the conclusion from the evidence."
