        "Treat When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next audit cycle as a control question: what would a reviewer need to repeat the check without asking? A sender who is offline should not receive a lead that needs an immediate response unless the lead can wait. Use a follow-the-sun rule or route urgent requests to an available sender. Document the rule and check the response times by region. Ask a reviewer who did not prepare the item to restate the conclusion from the evidence.",
        "Treat When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next audit cycle as a control question: what would a reviewer need to repeat the check without asking? A rising number of relationship exceptions may mean the rotation should be segmented by account ownership. A rising number of language exceptions may mean the team needs coverage in another market. Do not treat every exception as a problem, because some reflect real buyer needs. Leave the exception and the approver in the record instead of relying on memory."
